From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tab S9 FE Linux Project <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: input: novatek: return a valid IRQ status on resume failure

The threaded interrupt handler returned SEC_ERROR or a negative errno when a
resume wait failed.  Neither is a valid irqreturn_t.  The interrupt belongs to
this device and has been consumed even when its event must be dropped, so
report IRQ_HANDLED on both failure paths.

Signed-off-by: Tab S9 FE Linux Project <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek/nt36523_tablet_spi/nt36xxx.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek/nt36523_tablet_spi/nt36xxx.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek/nt36523_tablet_spi/nt36xxx.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek/nt36523_tablet_spi/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/novatek/nt36523_tablet_spi/nt36xxx.c
@@ -2765,12 +2765,12 @@ static irqreturn_t nvt_ts_work_func(int irq, void *data)
 		ret = wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(&ts->resume_done, msecs_to_jiffies(500));
 		if (ret == 0) {
 			input_err(true, &ts->client->dev, "%s: LPM: pm resume is not handled\n", __func__);
-			return SEC_ERROR;
+			return IRQ_HANDLED;
 		}
 
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			input_err(true, &ts->client->dev, "%s: LPM: -ERESTARTSYS if interrupted, %d\n", __func__, ret);
-			return ret;
+			return IRQ_HANDLED;
 		}
 
 		input_info(true, &ts->client->dev, "%s: run LPM interrupt handler, %d\n", __func__, ret);
-- 
